</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs for Algorithm <math id="A3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the proofs for algorithm <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math>, including the proofs for the connection to the RLHF-based procedure, suboptimality, and constraint violation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We note that our proofs for the connection between our DPO-based procedure and the RLHF-based procedure (Theorems <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title='Theorem 3 (Connection between Standard DPO and Standard RLHF with Constrained Policy Ranges). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title='Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title='Theorem 5 (Connection between Standard DPO and Standard RLHF with Constrained Policy Ranges and Exploration Bonuses). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title='Theorem 6 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF with Constrained Policy Ranges and Exploration Bonuses). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) follow the analysis of Proposition 4 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al.(2024)Azar, Guo, Piot, Munos, Rowland, Valko, and
Calandriello</a>]</cite>. We extend their analysis to the setting with constrained policy search ranges and a Lagrangian objective.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first give a result which builds a bridge between standard DPO and standard RLHF with constrained policy search ranges.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}:=[-R_{\max},R_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}:=[-R_{\max},R_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}:=[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}:=[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the following problem which first learns a reward model and then finds the optimal policy to maximize the learned reward function:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{r}\leftarrow\min_{r\in\mathcal{R}}\ -\frac{1}{N^{r}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\log\sigma\left(r(x_{i},y_{i}^{rw})-r(x_{i},y_{i}^{r\ell})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{r}\leftarrow\min_{r\in\mathcal{R}}\ -\frac{1}{N^{r}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\log\sigma\left(r(x_{i},y_{i}^{rw})-r(x_{i},y_{i}^{r\ell})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Connection between Standard DPO and Standard RLHF with Constrained Policy Ranges)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problems Eqs. (<a href="#S4.E15" title='In 1 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E20" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) have the same set of optimal solutions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step (i).<span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First, we prove that
if <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E20" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), then <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title='In 1 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E19" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), then <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}\in\Pi^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}\in\Pi^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> (as defined in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3 Preliminaries ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)) is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E20" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>). We have that <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title='In 1 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>). Otherwise, there exists another <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> which achieves a smaller objective value in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title='In 1 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>). Then, there must exist a <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}r^{\prime}(x,y)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}r^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})\right)}_{:=Z_{r^{\prime}}(x)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}r^{\prime}(x,y)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}r^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})\right)}_{:=Z_{r^{\prime}}(x)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\prime}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\prime}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the objective value in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E19" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) achieved by <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{r}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}}(x_{i})-\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{r}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}}(x_{i})-\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">is smaller than that achieved by <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which contradicts the supposition that <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E19" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step (ii).</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we prove that if <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title='In 1 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), then <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E20" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}\in\Pi^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}\in\Pi^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title='In 1 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), then there exists a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\pi}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}(x,y)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}(x,y^{\prime})\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\pi}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}(x,y)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}(x,y^{\prime})\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">i.e.,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{r}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{r}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We have that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the optimal value in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E19" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{r}}\!\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\!\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}\!+\!\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x_{i})\!-\!\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}\!+\!\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{r}}\!\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\!\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}_{i}|x_{i})}\!+\!\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x_{i})\!-\!\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}_{i}|x_{i})}\!+\!\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Otherwise, there exists another <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and then there exists a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}\in\Pi^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}\in\Pi^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> which gives a smaller objective value than <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E21" title='In Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).
Thus, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the optimal value in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E19" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>). Then, the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E20" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) under cost model <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\tilde{r}(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\propto}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∝</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\propto}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{\pi}(y|x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{\pi}(y|x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where (a) uses Eq. (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3 Preliminaries ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E20" title='In C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In the following, we provide a result which builds a connection between our rearranged Lagrangian DPO objective and the safe RLHF objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, problem Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title='In 3 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) and the following problem</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{c}\leftarrow\min_{c\in[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]}\ -\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\left(c(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-c(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{c}\leftarrow\min_{c\in[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]}\ -\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\left(c(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-c(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">have the same set of optimal solutions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title='Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> demonstrates that our rearranged Lagrangian DPO objective is an effective and alternative way to learn the optimal policy of maximizing the Lagrangian function, while enjoying the advantage of memory and computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title='Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, note that for any <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E23" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}(x,y^{\prime})-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(x)}},\ \forall x\in\mathcal{X}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}(x,y^{\prime})-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(x)}},\ \forall x\in\mathcal{X}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{c}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{c}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\hat{r}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\hat{r}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{=}\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}}(x)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(x)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{=}\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}}(x)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}(x)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">where equality (a) uses Eq. (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3 Preliminaries ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof consists of two steps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step (i).<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First, we prove that if <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E23" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), then <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title='In 3 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E22" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), then <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> (as shown in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E24" title='In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>)) is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E23" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>). We have that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}\hat{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title='In 3 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>). Otherwise, there exists another <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> which achieves a smaller objective value in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title='In 3 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>). Then, there must exist a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c^{\prime}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c^{\prime}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c^{\prime}(x,y)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c^{\prime}(x,y)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the objective value in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E22" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) achieved by <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x_{i})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 70.0001pt-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 70.0001pt-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">is smaller than that achieved by <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which contradicts the supposition that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E22" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step (ii).<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Next, we prove that if <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title='In 3 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), then <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E23" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>).</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title='In 3 ‣ 1 ‣ 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), then there exists a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{k}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y^{\prime}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{k}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y^{\prime}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)}-\lambda_{k}\cdot c_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{k}(x,y)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{k}(x,y)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">We have that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the optimal value in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E22" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x_{i})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{cw}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 50.00008pt-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 50.00008pt-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y_{i}^{c\ell}|x_{i})}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x_{i})\right)\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">Otherwise, there exists another <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and then there exists a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}-\lambda_{k}c^{\prime}}\in\Pi^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> which gives a smaller objective value than <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E25" title='In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>).
Thus, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the optimal value in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E22" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>). Then, the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E22" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) under cost model <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\Bigg(\frac{1}{\beta}\bigg(\hat{r}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\Bigg(\frac{1}{\beta}\bigg(\hat{r}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x)\bigg)\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x)\bigg)\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\propto}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}}(x)+\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x)\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∝</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\propto}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}}(x)+\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}c_{k}}(x)\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y|x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y|x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses Eq. (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3 Preliminaries ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A3.E23" title='In Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Cost Estimation for Lagrangian Multiplier Update</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the following, we bound the estimation error between <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math> in Line <a href="#algorithm1" title='In 4.2 A Provably Efficient Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> of Algorithm <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}:=\frac{\delta}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}:=\frac{\delta}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define events</p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\left\{\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}},\ \forall i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}],\forall k\in[K]\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\left\{\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}},\ \forall i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}],\forall k\in[K]\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\left\{\left|\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[c^{*}(x,y)\right]\right|\leq C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}},\ \forall k\in[K]\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\left\{\left|\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[c^{*}(x,y)\right]\right|\leq C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}},\ \forall k\in[K]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathcal{E}\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathcal{E}\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathcal{F}\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathcal{F}\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Hoeffding’s inequality, for any <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, for any fixed <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i})=(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i})=(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that with probability at least <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\tilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\tilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2}{\tilde{\delta}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2}{\tilde{\delta}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking a union bound over <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain the first statement.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the fact that <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}(x,y)\in[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}(x,y)\in[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, Hoeffding’s inequality, and a union bound over <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain the second statement.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that event <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right|\leq C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>W</mi><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right|\leq C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W:=\frac{1}{\left(\frac{1}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)\left(\frac{\exp(-C_{\max})}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}-\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W:=\frac{1}{\left(\frac{1}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)\left(\frac{\exp(-C_{\max})}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}-\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}:=\frac{\delta}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}:=\frac{\delta}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}(x,y)\in[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}(x,y)\in[-C_{\max},C_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(-C_{\max})-\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\bar{Z}_{i}\leq\sigma(C_{\max})+\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(-C_{\max})-\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\bar{Z}_{i}\leq\sigma(C_{\max})+\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The derivative of <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{-1}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{-1}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma^{-1})^{\prime}(z)=\frac{1}{z(1-z)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma^{-1})^{\prime}(z)=\frac{1}{z(1-z)}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> lying between <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\sigma^{-1})^{\prime}(z)\!\leq\!\frac{1}{\left(\frac{1}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}\!+\!\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)\!\!\left(\frac{\exp(-C_{\max})}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}\!-\!\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)}\!:=\!W." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.049em;" width="0.049em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">:=</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\sigma^{-1})^{\prime}(z)\!\leq\!\frac{1}{\left(\frac{1}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}\!+\!\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)\!\!\left(\frac{\exp(-C_{\max})}{1+\exp(-C_{\max})}\!-\!\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\right)}\!:=\!W.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">According to the Lagrange’s Mean Value Theorem, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})-c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})-c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})-\sigma^{-1}(\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})))\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})-\sigma^{-1}(\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})))\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq W\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq W\left|\bar{Z}_{i}-\sigma(c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i}))\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})-W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})\leq c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})-W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})\leq c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the above argument holds for any <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N^{\textup{CE}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})-W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})-W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}c^{*}(x_{i},y_{i})+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with the definition of event <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[c^{*}(x,y)\right]-C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}-W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[c^{*}(x,y)\right]-C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}-W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}\leq\frac{1}{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{\textup{CE}}}\sigma^{-1}(\bar{Z}_{i})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[c^{*}(x,y)\right]+C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>W</mi><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[c^{*}(x,y)\right]+C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{2|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Suboptimality and Constraint Violation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we give the proof of the suboptimality and constraint violation guarantees for Algorithm <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title='Theorem 1 (Result of Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾). ‣ 4.3 Theoretical Guarantees of Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that for any <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vector where the entry corresponding to <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and all other entries are <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, let</p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{r}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\left(\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{rw})-\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{r\ell})\right)\left(\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{rw})-\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{r\ell})\right)^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{i=1}^{N^{r}}\left(\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{rw})-\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{r\ell})\right)\left(\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{rw})-\phi(x^{r}_{i},y_{i}^{r\ell})\right)^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{c}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\left(\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right)\left(\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\left(\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right)\left(\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-\phi(x^{c}_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define event</p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{G}:=\Bigg\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>:=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{G}:=\Bigg\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|\hat{r}(x,y)-r^{*}(x,y)|\leq 4\left\|\phi(x,y)\right\|_{(\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{r}}+\gamma I)^{-1}}\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\hat{r}(x,y)-r^{*}(x,y)|\leq 4\left\|\phi(x,y)\right\|_{(\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{r}}+\gamma I)^{-1}}\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\left(\exp\left(R_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-R_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{2}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)\right)+\gamma(R_{\max})^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\left(\exp\left(R_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-R_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{2}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)\right)+\gamma(R_{\max})^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)|\leq 4\left\|\phi(x,y)\right\|_{(\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{c}}+\gamma I)^{-1}}\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)|\leq 4\left\|\phi(x,y)\right\|_{(\Sigma_{\mathcal{D}^{c}}+\gamma I)^{-1}}\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\left(\exp\left(C_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-C_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{2}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)\right)+\gamma(C_{\max})^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\left(\exp\left(C_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-C_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{2}{\delta^{\prime}}\right)\right)+\gamma(C_{\max})^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MLE Guarantee, Lemma 3.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al.(2023)Zhu, Jordan, and Jiao</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathcal{G}\right]\geq 1-2\delta^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathcal{G}\right]\geq 1-2\delta^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})-f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})\!\leq\!-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]+\lambda_{k}\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]\right)\!." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.608em;" width="0.608em"><mo lspace="0.108em">≤</mo></mpadded><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})-f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})\!\leq\!-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]+\lambda_{k}\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]\right)\!.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(b)}}{\leq}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(b)</mtext></mover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(b)}}{\leq}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda_{k}\cdot\hat{c}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]+\lambda_{k}\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]+\lambda_{k}\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where inequality (a) uses the fact that <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible, and inequality (b) comes from the definition of <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title='Theorem 4 (Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF). ‣ Step (ii). ‣ C.1 Connection between Our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now we prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title='Theorem 1 (Result of Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾). ‣ 4.3 Theoretical Guarantees of Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title='Theorem 1 (Result of Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾). ‣ 4.3 Theoretical Guarantees of Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ 4 Primal-Dual DPO Utilizing Standard DPO ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}:=\frac{\delta}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}:=\frac{\delta}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, according to Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma1" title='Lemma 1. ‣ C.2 Cost Estimation for Lagrangian Multiplier Update ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title='Lemma 3 (MLE Guarantee, Lemma 3.1 in []). ‣ C.3 Suboptimality and Constraint Violation ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}\cap\mathcal{G}]\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}\cap\mathcal{G}]\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, it suffices to prove this theorem assuming that event <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}\cap\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}\cap\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> holds. In the following proof, we assume that event <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}\cap\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\cap\mathcal{F}\cap\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\lambda}\in[0,2\rho]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\lambda}\in[0,2\rho]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\lambda^{k+1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\lambda^{k+1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\textup{Proj}_{[0,2\rho]}\left(\lambda_{k}+\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}\right)-\textup{Proj}_{[0,2\rho]}\left(\bar{\lambda}\right)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Proj</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Proj</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\textup{Proj}_{[0,2\rho]}\left(\lambda_{k}+\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}\right)-\textup{Proj}_{[0,2\rho]}\left(\bar{\lambda}\right)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}\left(\lambda_{k}+\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}\left(\lambda_{k}+\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+2\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)+\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+2\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)+\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where inequality (a) uses the nonexpansivity of the projection to <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,2\rho]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,2\rho]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing the above inequality over <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq\left(\lambda_{K+1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}\leq\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq\left(\lambda_{K+1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}\leq\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\tilde{c}_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\bar{\lambda}-\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]\cdot\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\bar{\lambda}-\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)]\cdot\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)\left(\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)\left(\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title='Lemma 4. ‣ C.3 Suboptimality and Constraint Violation ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Algorithm 𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\bar{\lambda}+f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})-f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\cdot\bar{\lambda}+f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})-f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\eta_{k}\right)^{2}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)\left(\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}2\eta_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)\left(\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}=\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}=\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi_{k})\right)+\bar{\lambda}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi_{k})\right)+\bar{\lambda}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2\eta}\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\frac{\eta}{2}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2\eta}\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\frac{\eta}{2}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\tilde{c}_{k}\right)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)\left(\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(\lambda_{k}-\bar{\lambda}\right)\left(\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}[\hat{c}(x,y)-c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})\right)-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi_{k})-f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi^{*};\hat{r})\right)-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi_{k})-f(\pi_{k};\hat{r})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2\eta}\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\frac{\eta(C_{\max})^{2}K}{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2\eta}\left(\lambda_{1}-\bar{\lambda}\right)^{2}+\frac{\eta(C_{\max})^{2}K}{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\lambda_{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
