<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">At the end of each iteration, <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> collects reward and cost preference feedback using <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and a baseline policy <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\textup{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\textup{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Line <a href="#algorithm2" title='In Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). The baseline policy <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\textup{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\textup{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed policy used in online preference data collection for ease of comparison. We make a technical assumption on <math id="A4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\textup{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\textup{base}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Baseline Policy)<span id="Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The baseline policy <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\textup{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\textup{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies that for any policy <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi,y^{\prime}\sim\pi^{\textup{base}}}\left[\left(\phi(x,y)-\phi(x,y^{\prime})\right)\left(\phi(x,y)-\phi(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi,y^{\prime}\sim\pi^{\textup{base}}}\left[\left(\phi(x,y)-\phi(x,y^{\prime})\right)\left(\phi(x,y)-\phi(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\succeq C^{\textup{base}}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y^{\prime}\sim\pi^{\textup{base}}}\left[\phi(x,y^{\prime})\phi(x,y^{\prime})^{\top}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\succeq C^{\textup{base}}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y^{\prime}\sim\pi^{\textup{base}}}\left[\phi(x,y^{\prime})\phi(x,y^{\prime})^{\top}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This assumption is used to guarantee that the difference of feature vectors between any policy <math id="A4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\textup{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\textup{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be connected to the feature vectors of <math id="A4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\textup{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\textup{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself, which is useful in analysis when bounding the error due to inferring reward and cost information from preference data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">After collecting online preference data, <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> adds these data to <math id="A4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{r}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{r}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, which will be used in model training in the next iteration (Line <a href="#algorithm2" title='In Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). As the algorithm proceeds, the preference data <math id="A4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{r}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{r}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> will cover more and more prompt-response space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proofs for Algorithm <math id="A5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the proofs for algorithm <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙿𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙳𝙿𝙾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{O\mbox{-}PD\mbox{-}DPO}</annotation></semantics></math> in the online data setting, including the proofs for the connection to the RLHF-based procedure, suboptimality, and constraint violation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we give a result which establishes a connection between standard DPO and standard RLHF with constrained policy search ranges and exploration bonuses.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define the following problem which first learns a reward model and then finds the optimal policy to maximize the learned reward with exploration bonuses:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{r}_{k}\leftarrow\min_{r\in\mathcal{R}}\ -\sum_{(x,y^{rw},y^{r\ell})\in\mathcal{D}^{r}_{k}}\log\sigma\left(r(x,y^{rw})-r(x,y^{r\ell})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{r}_{k}\leftarrow\min_{r\in\mathcal{R}}\ -\sum_{(x,y^{rw},y^{r\ell})\in\mathcal{D}^{r}_{k}}\log\sigma\left(r(x,y^{rw})-r(x,y^{r\ell})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right]-\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Connection between Standard DPO and Standard RLHF with Constrained Policy Ranges and Exploration Bonuses)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problems Eqs. (<a href="#A4.E29" title='In 3 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E36" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) have the same set of optimal solutions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step (i).<span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First, we prove that
if <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E36" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), then <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E29" title='In 3 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>).</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{k}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{k}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E35" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), then</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})+b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})+b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E36" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>). We have that <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E29" title='In 3 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>). Otherwise, there exists another <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{r}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{r}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> which achieves a smaller objective value in Eq. (<a href="#A4.E29" title='In 3 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>). Then, there must exist a <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(r^{\prime}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(r^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})+b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(r^{\prime}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(r^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})+b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\prime}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\prime}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">and the objective value in Eq. (<a href="#A5.E35" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) achieved by <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{(x,y^{rw},y^{r\ell})\in\tilde{\mathcal{D}}^{r}_{k}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{rw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{rw})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{(x,y^{rw},y^{r\ell})\in\tilde{\mathcal{D}}^{r}_{k}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{rw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{rw})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 100.00015pt-\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{r\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{r\ell})\right)\Bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 100.00015pt-\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{r\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{r^{\prime}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{r\ell})\right)\Bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">is smaller than that achieved by <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves a smaller DPO objective value),
which contradicts the supposition that <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E35" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step (ii).</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we prove that if <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E29" title='In 3 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E36" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E29" title='In 3 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), then there exists a <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies</p>
<table id="A5.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\pi}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}(x,y^{\prime})+b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\pi}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}(x,y^{\prime})+b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">i.e.,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{r}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{r}(x,y)=\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We have that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the optimal value in Eq. (<a href="#A5.E35" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A5.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{(x,y^{rw},y^{r\ell})\in\tilde{\mathcal{D}}^{r}_{k}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{rw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{rw})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{(x,y^{rw},y^{r\ell})\in\tilde{\mathcal{D}}^{r}_{k}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{rw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{rw}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{rw})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 110.00017pt-\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{r\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{r\ell})\right)\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 110.00017pt-\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y^{r\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{r\ell}|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)-b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{r\ell})\right)\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Otherwise, there exists another <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and then there exists a <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> which gives a smaller objective value than <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A5.E38" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>).
Thus, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the optimal value in Eq. (<a href="#A5.E35" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>). Then, the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E36" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) under cost model <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A5.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex120.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\tilde{r}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\propto}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∝</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\propto}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\tilde{r}}(x)\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{\pi}(y|x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{\pi}(y|x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where (a) uses Eq. (<a href="#A5.E37" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E36" title='In E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>).
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we present a result which relates our rearranged Lagrangian DPO objective to the safe RLHF objective with constrained policy search ranges and exploration bonuses.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, define the following problem that first learns a cost model and then finds the optimal policy for the Lagrangian function under <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{c}_{k}\leftarrow\min_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\ -\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\left(c(x_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-c(x_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{c}_{k}\leftarrow\min_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\ -\frac{1}{N^{c}}\sum_{i=1}^{N^{c}}\log\sigma\left(c(x_{i},y_{i}^{cw})-c(x_{i},y_{i}^{c\ell})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}\!}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\!-\!\lambda_{k}\left(\hat{c}_{k}(x,y)\!-\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right]\!-\!\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p}\!}\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\!-\!\lambda_{k}\left(\hat{c}_{k}(x,y)\!-\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right]\!-\!\beta\cdot\textup{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textup{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Connection between Our Rearranged Lagrangian DPO and Safe RLHF with Constrained Policy Ranges and Exploration Bonuses)<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, Problems Eqs. (<a href="#A4.E30" title='In 4 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E40" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) have the same set of optimal solutions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, note that for any <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E40" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(y|x)\!=\!\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\!\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)\!+\!b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\!-\!\lambda_{k}\left(\hat{c}(x,y)\!-\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\!\!\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\!\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\!+\!b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\!-\!\lambda_{k}\left(\hat{c}(x,y^{\prime})\!-\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(y|x)\!=\!\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\!\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)\!+\!b^{r}_{k}(x,y)\!-\!\lambda_{k}\left(\hat{c}(x,y)\!-\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\!\!\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\!\left(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\!+\!b^{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\!-\!\lambda_{k}\left(\hat{c}(x,y^{\prime})\!-\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 330.0005pt\forall x\in\mathcal{X}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 330.0005pt\forall x\in\mathcal{X}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{c}_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{c}_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex125.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\Bigg(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\Bigg(\hat{r}_{k}(x,y)+b^{r}_{k}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\Bigg)+b^{c}_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\Bigg)+b^{c}_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{=}\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{=}\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\Bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}+\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(x)-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\Bigg)+b^{c}_{k}(x,y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\beta\log Z_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\Bigg)+b^{c}_{k}(x,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">where equality (a) uses a similar derivation as Eq. (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3 Preliminaries ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we prove this theorem.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step (i).<span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First, we prove that if <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E40" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>), then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E30" title='In 4 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>).</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{k}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{k}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E39" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>), then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> (as shown in Eq. (<a href="#A5.E41" title='In Proof. ‣ Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>)) is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E40" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>). We have that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}-\lambda_{k}(\hat{c}_{k}-b^{c}_{k})}</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E30" title='In 4 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>). Otherwise, there exists another <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> which achieves a smaller objective value in Eq. (<a href="#A4.E30" title='In 4 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>). Then, there must exist a <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c^{\prime}(x,y)-b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})-b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\prime}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c^{\prime}(x,y)-b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)\right)}{\underbrace{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c^{\prime}(x,y^{\prime})-b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)\right)}_{:=Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c^{\prime}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c^{\prime}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex130.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+b^{c}_{k}(x,y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+b^{c}_{k}(x,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the objective value in Eq. (<a href="#A5.E39" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) achieved by <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{(x,y^{cw},y^{c\ell})\in\mathcal{D}^{c}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y^{cw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{cw}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{cw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{cw}|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{(x,y^{cw},y^{c\ell})\in\mathcal{D}^{c}}\log\sigma\Bigg(\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y^{cw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{cw}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{cw}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{cw}|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\!\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\bigg)\!+\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{cw})\!-\!\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y^{c\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{c\ell}|x)}\!-\!\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{c\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{c\ell}|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\!\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\bigg)\!+\!b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{cw})\!-\!\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}}\bigg(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y^{c\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{c\ell}|x)}\!-\!\beta\log\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y^{c\ell}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{c\ell}|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\bigg)-b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{c\ell})\Bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\beta\log Z_{\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}}-\lambda_{k}(c^{\prime}-b^{c}_{k})}(x)\bigg)-b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{c\ell})\Bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">is smaller than that achieved by <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which contradicts the supposition that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E39" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step (ii).<span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Next, we prove that if <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E30" title='In 4 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>), then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is also an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E40" title='In Step (ii). ‣ E.1 Connection between our DPO-based Procedure and the RLHF-based Procedure with Exploration Bonuses ‣ Appendix E Proofs for Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>).</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}\in\tilde{\Pi}^{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal solution to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E30" title='In 4 ‣ 2 ‣ Appendix D Pseudo-code and Detailed Description of Algorithm 𝙾⁢"-"⁢𝙿𝙳⁢"-"⁢𝙳𝙿𝙾 ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>), then there exists a <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{k}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c_{k}(x,y)-b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y^{\prime}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c_{k}(x,y^{\prime})-b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{k}(y|x)=\frac{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c_{k}(x,y)-b^{c}_{k}(x,y)\right)\right)\right)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)\cdot\exp\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi^{*}_{\hat{r}_{k}+b^{r}_{k}}(y^{\prime}|x)}{\pi_{\textup{ref}}(y^{\prime}|x)}-\lambda_{k}\left(c_{k}(x,y^{\prime})-b^{c}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)\right)\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">i.e.,</span></p>
