<div id="A5.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A5.SS2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\lambda}=2\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\lambda}=2\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex223"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K})+2\rho\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>K</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K})+2\rho\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex224"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi_{k})\right)+\frac{2\rho}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left(f(\pi^{*})-f(\pi_{k})\right)+\frac{2\rho}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.SS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the second statement of the theorem naturally holds; Otherwise, we can replace the term <math id="A5.SS2.p21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\rho\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\rho\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS2.p21.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\rho[\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\rho[\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> in the above inequality.
Then, using Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1 (Corollary 8.43 in []). ‣ Appendix F Technical Tools ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10 (Theorem 3.60 in []). ‣ Appendix F Technical Tools ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex225"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi^{\textup{out}}_{K}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex226"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{\max}}{4\rho\sqrt{K}}\left(\frac{\left(\lambda_{1}-2\rho\right)^{2}}{\lambda_{1}}+\lambda_{1}\right)+\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[b^{c}_{k}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{\max}}{4\rho\sqrt{K}}\left(\frac{\left(\lambda_{1}-2\rho\right)^{2}}{\lambda_{1}}+\lambda_{1}\right)+\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[b^{c}_{k}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex227"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{2K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left|\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right|+\frac{1}{\rho K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[b^{r}_{k}(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{2K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\left|\tilde{c}_{k}-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\right|+\frac{1}{\rho K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi_{k}(\cdot|x)}[b^{r}_{k}(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex228"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\Bigg(\frac{C_{\max}}{\rho\sqrt{K}}\left(\frac{\left(\lambda_{1}-2\rho\right)^{2}}{\lambda_{1}}+\lambda_{1}\right)+C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{K}{\delta}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\Bigg(\frac{C_{\max}}{\rho\sqrt{K}}\left(\frac{\left(\lambda_{1}-2\rho\right)^{2}}{\lambda_{1}}+\lambda_{1}\right)+C_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{K}{\delta}\right)}{N^{\textup{CE}}}}+W\sqrt{\frac{\log\left(\frac{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|N^{\textup{CE}}K}{\delta}\right)}{M^{\textup{CE}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex229"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sqrt{\frac{\left(\exp\left(C_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-C_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}}{N^{\textup{on}}}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{K}{\delta}\right)\right)+\gamma^{\textup{on}}(C_{\max})^{2}}\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em">⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sqrt{\frac{\left(\exp\left(C_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-C_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}}{N^{\textup{on}}}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{K}{\delta}\right)\right)+\gamma^{\textup{on}}(C_{\max})^{2}}\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex230"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|K\left(\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)+\frac{1}{C^{\textup{base}}}\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+C^{\textup{base}}K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>C</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|K\left(\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)+\frac{1}{C^{\textup{base}}}\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+C^{\textup{base}}K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex231"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{\rho}\sqrt{\frac{\left(\exp\left(R_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-R_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}}{N^{\textup{on}}}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{K}{\delta}\right)\right)+\gamma^{\textup{on}}(R_{\max})^{2}}\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>N</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em">⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{\rho}\sqrt{\frac{\left(\exp\left(R_{\max}\right)+\exp\left(-R_{\max}\right)+2\right)^{2}}{N^{\textup{on}}}\left(|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|+\log\left(\frac{K}{\delta}\right)\right)+\gamma^{\textup{on}}(R_{\max})^{2}}\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex232"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|K\left(\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)+\frac{1}{C^{\textup{base}}}\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+C^{\textup{base}}K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)\right)}\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="1.000em">OPEN</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>C</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|K\left(\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)+\frac{1}{C^{\textup{base}}}\log\left(\frac{\gamma^{\textup{on}}+|\mathcal{D}^{r}_{1}|+C^{\textup{base}}K}{|\mathcal{X}||\mathcal{Y}|\gamma^{\textup{on}}}\right)\right)}\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Technical Tools</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce several technical tools which are used in our analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="Thmlemma8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 8.42 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beck(2017)</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\lambda)\leq u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\lambda)\leq u</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex233"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda\leq\frac{u-f(\bar{\pi})}{-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda\leq\frac{u-f(\bar{\pi})}{-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\lambda)\leq u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\lambda)\leq u</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex234"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex234.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq q(\lambda)\geq f(\bar{\pi})-\lambda\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq q(\lambda)\geq f(\bar{\pi})-\lambda\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex235"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\lambda\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\leq u-f(\bar{\pi})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\lambda\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]\leq u-f(\bar{\pi}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex236"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda\leq\frac{u-f(\bar{\pi})}{-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda\leq\frac{u-f(\bar{\pi})}{-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of the optimal solutions to the dual problem <math id="A6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\lambda\geq 0}q(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\lambda\geq 0}q(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Corollary 8.43 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beck(2017)</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{*}\in\Lambda^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{*}\in\Lambda^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex237"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda^{*}\leq\frac{f(\pi^{*})-f(\bar{\pi})}{-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]}\leq\rho," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda^{*}\leq\frac{f(\pi^{*})-f(\bar{\pi})}{-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}[c^{*}(x,y)]}\leq\rho,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the second inequality comes from the definition of <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This corollary can be obtained by setting <math id="A6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> as the optimal value to the dual problem <math id="A6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\lambda\geq 0}q(\lambda)=f(\pi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\lambda\geq 0}q(\lambda)=f(\pi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma8" title="Lemma 8 (Theorem 8.42 in []). ‣ Appendix F Technical Tools ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A6.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g(\pi):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}[c(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\pi):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}^{p},y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}[c(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</p>
<table id="A6.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex238"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v(u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex238.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\max_{\pi}\left\{f(\pi):g(\pi)\leq u\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\max_{\pi}\left\{f(\pi):g(\pi)\leq u\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex239"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex239.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\left\{\pi:g(\pi)\leq u\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\left\{\pi:g(\pi)\leq u\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9</span></span><span id="Thmlemma9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 3.59 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beck(2017)</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{*}\in\Lambda^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{*}\in\Lambda^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex240"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v(0)+\lambda^{*}u\geq v(u)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v(0)+\lambda^{*}u\geq v(u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex241"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\pi)-\lambda^{*}g(\pi)\leq\max_{\pi}\left(f(\pi)-\lambda^{*}g(\pi)\right)=q(\lambda^{*})=f(\pi^{*})=v(0)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\pi)-\lambda^{*}g(\pi)\leq\max_{\pi}\left(f(\pi)-\lambda^{*}g(\pi)\right)=q(\lambda^{*})=f(\pi^{*})=v(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for any <math id="A6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in C(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in C(u)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex242"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v(0)+\lambda^{*}u\geq f(\pi)-\lambda^{*}\left(g(\pi)-u\right)\geq f(\pi)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v(0)+\lambda^{*}u\geq f(\pi)-\lambda^{*}\left(g(\pi)-u\right)\geq f(\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the above inequality holds for all <math id="A6.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in C(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in C(u)</annotation></semantics></math>, by maximizing <math id="A6.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A6.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in C(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in C(u)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for any <math id="A6.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx124" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex243"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v(0)+\lambda^{*}u\geq v(u)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v(0)+\lambda^{*}u\geq v(u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 10</span></span><span id="Thmlemma10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 3.60 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beck(2017)</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If a policy <math id="Thmlemma10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx125" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex244"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\pi^{*})-f(\tilde{\pi})+\rho^{\prime}[g(\tilde{\pi})]_{+}\leq L," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\pi^{*})-f(\tilde{\pi})+\rho^{\prime}[g(\tilde{\pi})]_{+}\leq L,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\prime}\geq 2\lambda^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\prime}\geq 2\lambda^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx126" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex245"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[g(\tilde{\pi})]_{+}\leq\frac{2L}{\rho^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[g(\tilde{\pi})]_{+}\leq\frac{2L}{\rho^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Theorem 3.59 in []). ‣ Appendix F Technical Tools ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we have that for any <math id="A6.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx127" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex246"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v(0)-v(u)\geq-\lambda^{*}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v(0)-v(u)\geq-\lambda^{*}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}:=[g(\tilde{\pi})]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}:=[g(\tilde{\pi})]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx128" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex247"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\rho^{\prime}-\lambda^{*}\right)\tilde{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\rho^{\prime}-\lambda^{*}\right)\tilde{u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex247.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\rho^{\prime}\tilde{u}+v(0)-v(\tilde{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\rho^{\prime}\tilde{u}+v(0)-v(\tilde{u})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex248"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}f(\pi^{*})-f(\tilde{\pi})+\rho^{\prime}\tilde{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}f(\pi^{*})-f(\tilde{\pi})+\rho^{\prime}\tilde{u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex249"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">where inequality (a) uses the fact that <math id="A6.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(0)=f(\pi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(0)=f(\pi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\tilde{u})\geq f(\tilde{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\tilde{u})\geq f(\tilde{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\prime}\geq 2\lambda^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\prime}\geq 2\lambda^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx129" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex250"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{u}\leq\frac{L}{\rho^{\prime}-\lambda^{*}}\leq\frac{L}{\rho^{\prime}-\frac{\rho^{\prime}}{2}}=\frac{2L}{\rho^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{u}\leq\frac{L}{\rho^{\prime}-\lambda^{*}}\leq\frac{L}{\rho^{\prime}-\frac{\rho^{\prime}}{2}}=\frac{2L}{\rho^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11</span></span><span id="Thmlemma11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1},\dots,\psi_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1},\dots,\psi_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional random vectors following distributions <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{1},\dots,\mathcal{B}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{1},\dots,\mathcal{B}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, and we have <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\psi_{k}\|\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\psi_{k}\|\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> positive definite matrix such that <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}(A_{0})\geq\{1,L^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}(A_{0})\geq\{1,L^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}=A_{0}+\sum_{i=1}^{k}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{i}\sim\mathcal{B}_{i}}[\psi_{i}\psi_{i}^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}=A_{0}+\sum_{i=1}^{k}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{i}\sim\mathcal{B}_{i}}[\psi_{i}\psi_{i}^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmlemma11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx130" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex251"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\leq 2\log\frac{\det(A_{K})}{\det(A_{0})}\leq 2\log\left(\frac{\left(\frac{\textup{trace}(A_{0})+KL^{2}}{d}\right)^{d}}{\det\left(A_{0}\right)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mtext>trace</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\leq 2\log\frac{\det(A_{K})}{\det(A_{0})}\leq 2\log\left(\frac{\left(\frac{\textup{trace}(A_{0})+KL^{2}}{d}\right)^{d}}{\det\left(A_{0}\right)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">This proof uses a similar analytical procedure as Lemma 11 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abbasi-Yadkori et al.(2011)Abbasi-Yadkori, Pál, and
Szepesvári</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx131" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex252"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\det\left(A_{K}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\det\left(A_{K}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex252.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\psi_{K}\psi_{K}^{\top}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\psi_{K}\psi_{K}^{\top}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}\right)\det\left(I+\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\psi_{K}\psi_{K}^{\top}\right]\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}\right)\det\left(I+\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\psi_{K}\psi_{K}^{\top}\right]\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex254"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}\right)\det\left(I+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\psi_{K}\left(\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\psi_{K}\right)^{\top}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}\right)\det\left(I+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\psi_{K}\left(\left(A_{K-1}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\psi_{K}\right)^{\top}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex255"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}\right)\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\|\psi_{K}\|^{2}_{(A_{K-1})^{-1}}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{K-1}\right)\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{K}\sim\mathcal{B}_{K}}\left[\|\psi_{K}\|^{2}_{(A_{K-1})^{-1}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex256"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{0}\right)\prod_{k=1}^{K}\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\det\left(A_{0}\right)\prod_{k=1}^{K}\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking logarithm on both sides, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx132" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex257"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\det\left(A_{K}\right)=\log\det\left(A_{0}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\det\left(A_{K}\right)=\log\det\left(A_{0}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}(A_{0})\geq\{1,L^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}(A_{0})\geq\{1,L^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A6.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the fact that <math id="A6.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq 2\log(1+x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq 2\log(1+x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx133" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex258"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex258.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log\left(1+\mathbb{E}_{\psi_{k}\sim\mathcal{B}_{k}}\left[\|\psi_{k}\|^{2}_{(A_{k-1})^{-1}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex259"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\log\frac{\det\left(A_{K}\right)}{\det\left(A_{0}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\log\frac{\det\left(A_{K}\right)}{\det\left(A_{0}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex260"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}2\log\left(\frac{\left(\frac{\textup{trace}(A_{0})+KL^{2}}{d}\right)^{d}}{\det\left(A_{0}\right)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(a)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mtext>trace</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\textup{(a)}}{\leq}2\log\left(\frac{\left(\frac{\textup{trace}(A_{0})+KL^{2}}{d}\right)^{d}}{\det\left(A_{0}\right)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">where inequality (a) uses the AM-GM inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 12</span></span><span id="Thmlemma12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma H.3 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agarwal et al.(2020)Agarwal, Henaff, Kakade, and Sun</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution of <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vectors which satisfies that <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\psi\|\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\psi\|\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\sim\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\sim\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1},\dots,\psi_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1},\dots,\psi_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples from <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\mathbb{E}_{\psi\sim\mathcal{B}}[\psi\psi^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\mathbb{E}_{\psi\sim\mathcal{B}}[\psi\psi^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for any <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx134" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex261"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|v^{\top}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\psi_{i}\psi_{i}^{\top}-A\right)v\right|\leq\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{8\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{8\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|v^{\top}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\psi_{i}\psi_{i}^{\top}-A\right)v\right|\leq\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{8\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{8\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}:=\frac{\textup{trace}(A)}{\|A\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>trace</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}:=\frac{\textup{trace}(A)}{\|A\|}</annotation></semantics></math> is the intrinsic dimension of <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A6.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A6.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}:=\psi_{i}\psi_{i}^{\top}-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}:=\psi_{i}\psi_{i}^{\top}-A</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have that <math id="A6.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[D_{i}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[D_{i}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|D_{i}\|\leq L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|D_{i}\|\leq L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx135" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex262"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right\|\leq ML^{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right\|\leq ML^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">The intrinsic dimension of <math id="A6.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to that of <math id="A6.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, which is <math id="A6.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by definition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the Matrix Bernstein inequality (Theorem 7.7.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tropp et al.(2015)</a>]</cite>), we have that for any <math id="A6.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq L^{2}\sqrt{M}+\frac{L^{2}}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq L^{2}\sqrt{M}+\frac{L^{2}}{3}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx136" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex263"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\sigma_{\max}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right)\geq t\right]\leq 4\hat{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{-\frac{t^{2}}{2}}{L^{4}M+\frac{L^{2}t}{3}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\sigma_{\max}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right)\geq t\right]\leq 4\hat{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{-\frac{t^{2}}{2}}{L^{4}M+\frac{L^{2}t}{3}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Setting <math id="A6.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}=\frac{t}{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}=\frac{t}{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for any <math id="A6.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}\geq\frac{L^{2}}{\sqrt{M}}+\frac{L^{2}}{3M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}\geq\frac{L^{2}}{\sqrt{M}}+\frac{L^{2}}{3M}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx137" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex264"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\sigma_{\max}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right)\geq t^{\prime}\right]\leq 4\hat{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{-\frac{M(t^{\prime})^{2}}{2}}{L^{4}+\frac{L^{2}t^{\prime}}{3}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\sigma_{\max}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right)\geq t^{\prime}\right]\leq 4\hat{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{-\frac{M(t^{\prime})^{2}}{2}}{L^{4}+\frac{L^{2}t^{\prime}}{3}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A6.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}=\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}=\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\hat{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{-\frac{M(t^{\prime})^{2}}{2}}{L^{4}+\frac{L^{2}t^{\prime}}{3}}\right)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\hat{d}\cdot\exp\left(\frac{-\frac{M(t^{\prime})^{2}}{2}}{L^{4}+\frac{L^{2}t^{\prime}}{3}}\right)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, with probability at least <math id="A6.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx138" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex265"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{\max}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right)\leq\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{\max}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{E}[(D_{i})^{2}]\right)\leq\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{4\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can obtain this concentration inequality in the other direction with a similar argument. Therefore, we complete the proof of this lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 13</span></span><span id="Thmlemma13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma H.4 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agarwal et al.(2020)Agarwal, Henaff, Kakade, and Sun</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{1},\dots,\mathcal{B}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{1},\dots,\mathcal{B}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> distributions of <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vectors. For any <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, we draw <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i,1},\dots,\psi_{i,M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i,1},\dots,\psi_{i,M}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and form <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\psi_{i,j}\psi_{i,j}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\psi_{i,j}\psi_{i,j}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\psi\sim\mathcal{B}_{i}}[\psi\psi^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\psi\sim\mathcal{B}_{i}}[\psi\psi^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\sum_{i=1}^{K}A_{i}+\gamma I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\sum_{i=1}^{K}A_{i}+\gamma I</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}\hat{A}_{i}+\gamma I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}\hat{A}_{i}+\gamma I</annotation></semantics></math>. Setting <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=\frac{32K^{2}\ln(\frac{8K\tilde{d}}{\delta})}{\gamma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=\frac{32K^{2}\ln(\frac{8K\tilde{d}}{\delta})}{\gamma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for any <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx139" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex266"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v\leq v^{\top}(\hat{A}+\gamma I)^{-1}v\leq 2v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v\leq v^{\top}(\hat{A}+\gamma I)^{-1}v\leq 2v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{d}:=\max_{i\in[K]}\frac{\textup{trace}(A_{i})}{\|A_{i}\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>trace</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{d}:=\max_{i\in[K]}\frac{\textup{trace}(A_{i})}{\|A_{i}\|}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(M)=:\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{8K\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{8K\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(M)=:\frac{2L^{2}\ln\left(\frac{8K\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{3M}+L^{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln\left(\frac{8K\hat{d}}{\delta}\right)}{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma12" title="Lemma 12 (Lemma H.3 in []). ‣ Appendix F Technical Tools ‣ Primal-Dual Direct Preference Optimizationfor Constrained LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, we have that with probability <math id="A6.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A6.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx140" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex267"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{i}+\alpha(M)I+\frac{\gamma}{K}I\succeq\hat{A}_{i}+\frac{\gamma}{K}I\succeq A_{i}-\alpha(M)I+\frac{\gamma}{K}I." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{i}+\alpha(M)I+\frac{\gamma}{K}I\succeq\hat{A}_{i}+\frac{\gamma}{K}I\succeq A_{i}-\alpha(M)I+\frac{\gamma}{K}I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx141" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex268"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A+K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\succeq\hat{A}+\gamma I\succeq A-K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A+K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\succeq\hat{A}+\gamma I\succeq A-K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p21.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p21.3.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A6.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\geq 2K\alpha(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\geq 2K\alpha(M)</annotation></semantics></math>, the above inequality implies</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx142" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex269"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex269.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(A+K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\right)^{-1}\preceq\left(\hat{A}+\gamma I\right)^{-1}\preceq\left(A-K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\right)^{-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(A+K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\right)^{-1}\preceq\left(\hat{A}+\gamma I\right)^{-1}\preceq\left(A-K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\right)^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\Lambda U^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\Lambda U^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be the eigendecomposition of <math id="A6.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=\textup{diag}(\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\textup{diag}(\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=[u_{1},\dots,u_{d}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=[u_{1},\dots,u_{d}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx143" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex270"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{\top}(\hat{A}+\gamma I)^{-1}v-v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{\top}(\hat{A}+\gamma I)^{-1}v-v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex270.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq v^{\top}\left(\left(A-K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\right)^{-1}-(A+\gamma I)^{-1}\right)v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq v^{\top}\left(\left(A-K\alpha(M)I+\gamma I\right)^{-1}-(A+\gamma I)^{-1}\right)v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex271"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(\left(\sigma_{i}+\gamma-K\alpha(M)\right)^{-1}-\left(\sigma_{i}+\gamma\right)^{-1}\right)(v^{\top}u_{i})^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(\left(\sigma_{i}+\gamma-K\alpha(M)\right)^{-1}-\left(\sigma_{i}+\gamma\right)^{-1}\right)(v^{\top}u_{i})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A6.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A6.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}+\gamma\geq 2K\alpha(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}+\gamma\geq 2K\alpha(M)</annotation></semantics></math>, and then <math id="A6.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(\sigma_{i}+\gamma-K\alpha(M))\geq\sigma_{i}+\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(\sigma_{i}+\gamma-K\alpha(M))\geq\sigma_{i}+\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A6.p23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma_{i}+\gamma-K\alpha(M))^{-1}\leq 2(\sigma_{i}+\gamma)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma_{i}+\gamma-K\alpha(M))^{-1}\leq 2(\sigma_{i}+\gamma)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx144" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex272"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{\top}(\hat{A}+\gamma I)^{-1}v-v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v\leq\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(\sigma_{i}+\gamma\right)^{-1}(v^{\top}u_{i})^{2}=v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{\top}(\hat{A}+\gamma I)^{-1}v-v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v\leq\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(\sigma_{i}+\gamma\right)^{-1}(v^{\top}u_{i})^{2}=v^{\top}(A+\gamma I)^{-1}v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using a similar analysis, we can obtain the statement in the other direction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
